This document creates the ROS2 workspace and Python package that the rest of Lesson Set 01 (and later sets) will use.

1. Create the workspace
 mkdir -p ~/droidworks_ws/src
 cd ~/droidworks_ws

2. Create the Python package
From inside the src folder:
 cd ~/droidworks_ws/src
 ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_python droidworks_sensors
This creates a package named droidworks_sensors.

All Lesson Set 01 nodes will live inside this package for now.

3. Basic package layout
After creation you should have something like this:
 droidworks_sensors/
 ├── droidworks_sensors/
 │   └── __init__.py
 ├── package.xml
 ├── resource/
 │   └── droidworks_sensors
 ├── setup.cfg
 ├── setup.py
 └── test/

4. Key files you will edit
package.xml
 Update description, maintainer, and license if desired.
 Make sure these dependencies are present (add them if missing):
  <depend>rclpy</depend>
  <depend>std_msgs</depend>

setup.py
  This is where you will register every node as an entry point.
  You will add lines like this later:
    entry_points={
        'console_scripts': [
            'pir_entry = droidworks_sensors.pir_entry:main',
            'rcwl_entry = droidworks_sensors.rcwl_entry:main',
            # more nodes will be added here
        ],
    },

setup.cfg
 Usually needs no changes for our purposes.

5. First build and source
 From the workspace root:
  cd ~/droidworks_ws
  colcon build
  source install/setup.bash

You should now be able to run:
 ros2 pkg list | grep droidworks
and see droidworks_sensors.

Notes
 Keep the package name droidworks_sensors for the entire Lesson Set 01.
 We will place individual node files inside droidworks_sensors/droidworks_sensors/.
 Every time you add a new node, you must:
  Create the .py file
  Add the entry point in setup.py
  Run colcon build
  Source again

This workspace and package are the foundation.
